 "_notes": {
  "II.B": "Hypoxia types have no AIM taxonomy; card 0 uses 8-1-2 a.1/a.4 causes (CO, anemia, alcohol, drugs). AIM TUC figures differ from the card (8-1-2 a.3: 20-30 min at 18,000, 5-12 min at 20,000). Card 19 maps only the vitamin A / dark adaptation block (8-1-6 b.2); dehydration not in this AIM. Alcohol: AIM recommends 12-24 hr bottle to throttle (8-1-1 d.2). IMSAFE = 8-1-1 h/i personal checklist.",
  "II.C": "VOR checks 1-1-4 (91.411 not covered). No 91.169 alternate weather minimums in this edition; card 13 uses preflight briefing 5-1-1 a + high-altitude alternate caution 5-1-10. 91.175(j) = 5-4-9 b.1, OM substitutes (k) = 1-1-9 a.4. En route low chart block 9-1-4 b.1 skipped (garbled with helicopter chart text); 5-3-5 a/a.2 (91.181) skipped (mixed text).",
  "II.D": "No AIM content on logbook entries, endorsements or instructor records.",
